{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 RCA (pre-fix): Step 0(a) searched `completion sidecar material fingerprint COMPLETION_VERDICT material=None` and reviewed open/in_progress bug inventory; no duplicate found beyond this ticket. Related closed bug `panoramic-smallish-bullfrog` concerns stale-material grandfathering, not this missing-record defect. Step 0(b) report floor from created_at 1788224470982895037 is code sha 1d9193332139894cc46f5e7385e070d8bd06d5a2; current suspect files have no changes after that floor. Step 0(c) worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/compl-sidecar` is current at origin/main 1299d9deb6da82708bf694e19572ef8579664f34.\n\nConfirmed mechanism: the completion close helper `_emit_completion_sidecar` still invokes `completion_sidecar.emit(result, material=None, repo_root=repo_root)` (`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:405`), and standalone `record_completion_verdict` does the same (`src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:240`). `completion_sidecar.build_payload` stores only the `material` argument into `material_fingerprint` and ignores the verdict's existing `material_fingerprint` and `completion_read_basis`; a runtime probe of `build_payload({... material_fingerprint: 'abc123', completion_read_basis: ...})` returned `material_fingerprint: null` while preserving the read basis. The verifier path already computes the missing ingredients: `_attach_completion_read_basis` writes `result['material_fingerprint'] = current_material_fingerprint(...)` and `result['completion_read_basis'] = ticket_view.completion_basis(...).to_dict()` after a pinned ticket view records exact ticket observations. Therefore the sidecar record drops available verifier-input identity at the final emitter boundary; this is a record-enrichment omission, not a gate-outcome behavior change.\n\nDefect legitimacy: incomplete-implementation by operator-directed filing (2026-08-31) and by the originating sidecar plan's own scope, which required the sidecar to include \"the ticket's material fingerprint at verify time.\" Origin attribution: `git blame`/`git log -S'material=None'` point the initial completion-verifier sidecar emit path to commit 2830f30f58ea61807ad96adc1257be04bebd3fa2 (`rebar-ticket: 24ec-c291-9f47-47fd`, alias `olivine-married-kodiakbear`), whose ticket introduced FAIL sidecars and explicitly scoped a material fingerprint. PASS and standalone paths later copied/extended the same omission (e7e0, d123), but 24ec is the scope-of-work source for the completion-sidecar capability gap. Planned close class: `plan_defect`, caused_by `olivine-married-kodiakbear`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788233849522888001,"uuid":"5082401e-764c-49b9-bf00-a36bf11d3e6d"}